<title>ITALY: Lira eases versus mark, Bank Italy checking prices.</title>
<headline>Lira eases versus mark, Bank Italy checking prices.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian lira eased against the mark in line with a weaker French franc and Spanish peseta in a nervous market and the Bank of Italy had been asking prices, forex traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Bank was just checking on a routine basis at no specific level. It hasn't been seen intervening,&quot; one said.</p>
<p>At 0909 GMT, the lira was quoted at 994.65/4.95 per mark after touching a low at 995.25.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
